# What EAS Build uploads. When this file exists EAS uses it INSTEAD of
# .gitignore, and it does not read apps/mobile/.gitignore at all — so every
# rule the upload needs is here. Without it, the local android/ project and
# its build output (over a gigabyte) were uploaded and EAS skipped prebuild.

# Operating system and editors
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/

# Node, Expo and React Native
**/node_modules/
**/.expo/
**/.turbo/
**/dist/
**/web-build/
*.log
*.tmp
*.temp
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.metro-health-check*

# Native projects are generated on the build server by prebuild
apps/mobile/android/
apps/mobile/ios/
apps/mobile/.kotlin/

# Environment files: EAS builds read the EAS environment, never .env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Credentials and signing files (EAS holds these)
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
*.mobileprovision
credentials.json
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist

# Not needed to build the app
services/
docs/
*.md
compose.yaml
render.yaml
**/bin/
**/obj/
